---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { withBase } from "../../lib/paths";
---

<BaseLayout title="AreaClicker - Windows desktop tool in Rust" sideBarActiveItemID="projects">
  <article class="grid gap-10">
    <header class="grid gap-4">
      <a class="link w-fit" href={withBase("/projects")}>Back to projects</a>
      <img src={withBase("/post_img.webp")} alt="Project preview" class="max-h-64 w-full rounded-lg object-cover" />
      <div>
        <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold">Personal helper tool for prototype testing</h1>
        <p class="mt-3 text-lg text-base-content/75">
          Windows Mouse movement scripting program for UI soak tests (archived).
        </p>
      </div>
    </header>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-3">Project Overview</h2>
      <p>
        Developped fully in Rust with an interface of egui, AreaClicker allows scripting repetitive mouse movements over user-selected areas (multiple screens possible) for long running UI soak tests. Click areas are compiled into sequences and subsequently validated before execution (bound checks, cycle detection, delay normalization). AreaClicker was developped for an extracurricular project in mind that was later dropped.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-3">Implementation</h2>
      <p>
        Rust's strong enum types were used for strict states of actions and objects. Areas are user entered via a selection from display, as well as further customization of sequenced clicks and wait times. To ensure robustness through lengthy run states, time intervals are periodically divided for task waiting allowing interoperability and fluid processor sharing.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-3">Tools and Technologies</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc mx-6 grid gap-2">
        <li>Rust desktop stack with eframe/egui for UI, Enigo for mouse control, winit/display-info for window and monitor handling, and serde/TOML for saved presets.</li>
        <li>Cargo-based builds and tests, Rust unit tests, compiled run-plan validation, recursive sequence detection, bounds validation, delay normalization, and optional rdev hotkey hooks</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-3">Links and Media</h2>
      <p>
        <div>
        <div class="font-bold">GitHub</div>
        <a href="https://github.com/michaeldmussel/AreaPicker" target="_blank">AreaPicker</a>
      </div>
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
